# LF in the repository AND in the worktree, on every platform.
#
# Without this the checkout obeys `core.autocrlf`, which is `true` on a stock Git for Windows and on
# GitHub's windows-latest runners — so every text file lands with CRLF. The suite still RUNS, because
# MSYS2's bash ignores a trailing CR, which is exactly what made this hard to see: it fails only where
# bytes are COMPARED rather than executed. tools/check-grammar.sh diffs the CRLF docs/grammar.bnf in the
# worktree against the LF file tools/gen-grammar just wrote, all 1272 lines differ, and the guard reports
# "the grammar is stale" — a true-looking answer to a question nobody asked. `text=auto` still leaves
# binary files (assets, .vsix, .png) alone; git detects those itself.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Kama is the point of this repo — keep the GitHub language bar reading as Kama.
# The benchmark comparison sources and the parked LLVM backend are not the project's
# code; mark them vendored so they don't dominate the stats. The C++ compiler sources
# stay counted — that's the honest implementation language.
bench/src/c/**       linguist-vendored
bench/src/cpp/**     linguist-vendored
bench/src/go/**      linguist-vendored
bench/src/rust/**    linguist-vendored
bench/src/java/**    linguist-vendored
bench/src/csharp/**  linguist-vendored
bench/src/lua/**     linguist-vendored
bench/src/ts/**      linguist-vendored
bench/src/js/**      linguist-vendored
bench/src/python/**  linguist-vendored
legacy-llvm/**       linguist-vendored

# The tree-sitter parser is GENERATED from tree-sitter-kama/grammar.js — tens of
# thousands of lines of machine-written C that would otherwise swamp the language bar
# and show up in every diff review. grammar.js itself stays counted; it's the source.
tree-sitter-kama/src/**  linguist-generated=true

# Until Linguist ships a Kama entry this is a harmless no-op; once it lands, `.kama`
# files classify as Kama on github.com. (Not `linguist-language=C` — that would
# mislabel .kama as C in the stats.)
*.kama               linguist-language=Kama
